WEBVTT

00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:31.676
They're really in their own head

00:30:31.700 --> 00:30:35.311
and like, "I have
a meeting to get to. Bye."

00:30:35.335 --> 00:30:37.834
Like, "Welcome to Brooklyn." (Laughs)

00:30:37.858 --> 00:30:42.076
Man in office: Right? Like,
the loneliness thing is very real ...

00:30:42.100 --> 00:30:45.286
AG: Coworking spaces are
an extreme place to look at loneliness.

00:30:45.310 --> 00:30:47.977
People often go there
searching for a sense of community

00:30:48.001 --> 00:30:51.017
but find that they have little in common
with those around them.

00:30:51.041 --> 00:30:52.835
They may not work on a team together,

00:30:52.859 --> 00:30:54.357
belong to the same organization

00:30:54.381 --> 00:30:56.578
or share a mission and culture.

00:30:56.602 --> 00:31:00.126
Ironically, it can be lonelier
than working alone.